F-1 (Foxy portability): build the fork on ROS 2 Foxy as well as Humble.

The G1's onboard computer runs Foxy (Ubuntu 20.04); this workspace was
written on Humble (Ubuntu 22.04) and the simulator stays there. Nothing in
this patch changes what the extractor, tracker or publisher COMPUTE — every
hunk is a spelling that Foxy's rclcpp/tf2/rosidl accept and Humble's still
accept. Verified by building the same tree under both distros (Foxy in the
focal container of ros2/docker/foxy, Humble natively).

The four incompatibilities, in the order the compiler found them:

1. CMake. `rosidl_get_typesupport_target()` is Galactic+. Foxy's equivalent
   is `rosidl_target_interfaces()`. Selected with `if(COMMAND ...)` so the
   file works on either, rather than being pinned to one distro.

2. tf2_geometry_msgs. Foxy ships `tf2_geometry_msgs.h`; the `.hpp` spelling
   arrived in Galactic. Selected with `__has_include`. Separately, Foxy
   specializes `doTransform` only for the *Stamped* message types — there is
   no unstamped `Pose` overload, which is what `transformPoint()` called, so
   the shared library built and the executable failed to link. Rewritten to
   the `PoseStamped` form, which exists on both distros and which Humble
   implements by forwarding to the unstamped one: same arithmetic, same
   returned position.

3. Parameters. `declare_parameter(name, rclcpp::ParameterType)` — declare by
   type with no default — arrived with rclcpp 16 (Humble). Foxy expresses
   the same intent as `declare_parameter(name)`, which leaves the parameter
   PARAMETER_NOT_SET. Both leave it unset when no override is supplied,
   which is exactly what the `get_parameter_or(name, out, default)` calls
   that follow every declaration rely on. Routed through
   `obstacle_detector::declare_parameter_typed()` in the new
   utilities/rclcpp_compat.h so the 46 call sites read the same on both.

4. Subscription callbacks. rclcpp accepts `const MessageT&` callbacks only
   from Galactic on, and Foxy's subscription traits do not deduce the
   message type through a `const ConstSharedPtr&` parameter either. The
   subscriptions now pass a ConstSharedPtr-by-value lambda that forwards to
   the existing callback — scanCallback(), pclCallback(), odomCallback() and
   obstaclesCallback() keep their signatures and their bodies verbatim.

Applies on top of patches 0003 + 0004 + 0007 + 0009 + 0010 AND the
A-mode `loop_rate` revival that currently lives only in the working tree
(obstacle_tracker.{h,cpp}, uncommitted, no patch of its own — it reactivates
what 0010 retired, for the rate-comparison experiment). Verified by
reconstructing the pre-image of the five touched files, applying this patch,
and diffing the result against the working tree: identical. On a bare
0003..0010 stack the two obstacle_tracker.cpp hunks will need re-anchoring —
that drift predates this patch.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -35,6 +35,21 @@
   DEPENDENCIES geometry_msgs std_msgs builtin_interfaces 
 )
 
+# Link a target against this package's OWN generated messages, on both Foxy
+# and Humble. rosidl_get_typesupport_target() does not exist before Galactic;
+# Foxy's equivalent is rosidl_target_interfaces(), which resolves and links the
+# generated typesupport into the target directly. Same libraries either way —
+# only the CMake spelling differs.
+function(obstacle_detector_link_own_messages target)
+  if(COMMAND rosidl_get_typesupport_target)
+    rosidl_get_typesupport_target(cpp_typesupport_target
+      "${PROJECT_NAME}" "rosidl_typesupport_cpp")
+    target_link_libraries(${target} "${cpp_typesupport_target}")
+  else()
+    rosidl_target_interfaces(${target} ${PROJECT_NAME} "rosidl_typesupport_cpp")
+  endif()
+endfunction()
+
